1
00:00:00,965 --> 00:00:03,390
Morning… and the doors are open.

2
00:00:04,023 --> 00:00:08,408
In Eikon, Today's team says who is in, until when,

3
00:00:08,448 --> 00:00:10,743
and which pharmacist is in charge.

4
00:00:11,604 --> 00:00:13,409
Ryan starts on Monday.

5
00:00:13,469 --> 00:00:16,769
Plan shifts, fill, a usual week or rotation.

6
00:00:17,953 --> 00:00:20,718
Three afternoons, and every other Saturday.

7
00:00:21,383 --> 00:00:23,928
Save it, and see what it will do:

8
00:00:23,968 --> 00:00:27,933
a whole year of shifts, public holidays skipped.

9
00:00:28,645 --> 00:00:31,065
Add them. Changed your mind?

10
00:00:31,170 --> 00:00:34,665
Undo takes them all off again, in one step.

11
00:00:35,327 --> 00:00:36,912
A day with no pharmacist,

12
00:00:36,952 --> 00:00:39,672
or more hours than the contract?

13
00:00:40,002 --> 00:00:42,332
It says so… before it happens.

14
00:00:43,407 --> 00:00:46,382
On his phone, Karl sees his own shifts,

15
00:00:46,422 --> 00:00:48,662
and who he works with.

16
00:00:49,289 --> 00:00:50,289
Add to my calendar…

17
00:00:50,329 --> 00:00:53,469
and a note whenever his shifts change.

18
00:00:54,358 --> 00:00:56,668
And what the last shift left him:

19
00:00:56,708 --> 00:00:58,418
read it, got it.

20
00:00:59,306 --> 00:01:02,846
Eikon. The right people, in the right place.

